# Staging → main changelog

A PR from `staging` into `main` is a production release. Before opening or merging it:

1. Diff `origin/main...origin/staging`.
2. Write a short PR summary of **reader-facing** changes (what someone on a Kindle would notice). Skip chores, CI, deploy wiring, and refactors unless they change behaviour.
3. Prepend a dated entry to `src/main/resources/templates/changelog.html` (newest first). Use today's date. Keep bullets plain and specific. Do not rewrite older entries.

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD — prepend this article above existing ones -->
<article class="changelog-entry">
  <h2>31 August 2026</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Feeds can be renamed from the category row.</li>
    <li>Send-to-Kindle stays on the current article page instead of jumping away.</li>
  </ul>
</article>

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<article class="changelog-entry">
  <h2>Update</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Various fixes and improvements.</li>
    <li>Bump CI and Railway config.</li>
  </ul>
</article>
```

If nothing user-visible shipped, say so in the PR body and **do not** add a changelog article.
